      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two cases of ectopic pregnancy are presented in which acute urinary retention was a salient clinical feature. The emergency physician must consider ectopic pregnancy in the differential diagnosis in any woman of child-bearing age with abdominal, pelvic, or urinary complaints."},
